    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2U9j5hzSNzpqaW8cZvVNEHC)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main`; no dependency. Touches only `sp-embark` (`.el` and its literate doc).\n- Branch is `484-embark-keys`: the number was predicted (last PR was #483); if GitHub gave another number, tell me.\n\n## Changes\n\n- New map `lem+embark-keys` on the leader, `C-; E` (`E` was free; `e` is eval):\n  - `a` act, `A` act-all, `s` select, `c` collect, `l` live, `e` export, `b` become, `d` dwim, `B` bindings.\n- `C-,` in `minibuffer-local-map` is `embark-select`, to mark candidates fast.\n- Works in the minibuffer too, since the leader is global.\n- No `C-z`, `C-x`, `C-c`, `C-v`, `C-SPC` or `s-SPC` (clipboard keys, input-source switch, Alfred). GUI keys only.\n- Docs as bullets in `docs/tangles/tooling/sp-embark.org`. No CHANGELOG edit.\n\n## Choices and alternatives\n\n- Chose a leader submenu over new global roots. Alternatives:\n  - Bind inside `embark-general-map` (only reachable after `C-.`, which already offers these keys).\n  - A dedicated minibuffer-only key set (kept just `C-,` for select).\n  - Put the map in `sp-keys` instead of `sp-embark`.\n- `C-,` was free in my search of the modules; Org and some packages bind it locally.\n\n## Not tested\n\n- No Emacs in the container: nothing was loaded or run, and `tools/check-tangle.sh` was not run.\n- Not checked that `C-; E` is free in every mode.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 484-embark-keys; git checkout 484-embark-keys`, restart Emacs\n- [x] `C-; E` shows the map in which-key\n- [ ] `M-x find-file`, then `C-,` on a candidate: it is marked; `C-; E A` runs an action on all marked\n- [x] `C-; E c` and `C-; E e` in a minibuffer prompt open a collect and an export buffer\n- [ ] `C-; E s` outside the minibuffer selects the target at point\n- [ ] `C-.` and `M-.` still work\n- [ ] In an Org buffer `C-,` is unchanged (minibuffer only)\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main && git -C ~/dotfiles pull`; restart Emacs.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDP4jhu4cC46YFafhr)_",
